      "versionNonce": 450716214,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788952711882,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. getMessage() : It is a method of Throwable which return\nstring with a message for the reason/cause of the exception .\n\n2. toString() : This method belongs to Object class .\nIt is defined in such a way whenever we pass ref to print() it\nreturns hashcode of that object .\n\nSo java strongly recommends us to override the toString() so\nthat it return the object data in the form of string .\n\n\nMany in built classes has overriden toString() method like String,\nDate etc .\n\nException classes has also overriden toString such that it\nreturns two things \n\n   a. Exception class name \n   b. Error Message\n\n3. printStackTrace \n\n--> It belongs to Throwable \n--> Whenever we call it it returns 5 things \n1. Exception class name \n2. error message \n3. method name\n4. File name\n5. line number",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. getMessage() : It is a method of Throwable which return string with a message for the reason/cause of the exception .\n\n2. toString() : This method belongs to Object class .\nIt is defined in such a way whenever we pass ref to print() it returns hashcode of that object .\n\nSo java strongly recommends us to override the toString() so that it return the object data in the form of string .\n\n\nMany in built classes has overriden toString() method like String, Date etc .\n\nException classes has also overriden toString such that it returns two things \n\n   a. Exception class name \n   b. Error Message\n\n3. printStackTrace \n\n--> It belongs to Throwable \n--> Whenever we call it it returns 5 things \n1. Exception class name \n2. error message \n3. method name\n4. File name\n5. line number",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
